      "block": "Default classification for every cell not reached by a street buffer. This is a simplification: no separate OSM building-footprint query was run (block == 'not street'), since for a game-grid contract that is sufficient to make cells walkable/blocked; the art team can subdivide 'block' cells with building art freely without touching walkability.",
      "landmark": "A fixed 3x3 tile footprint (30m x 30m) centered exactly on the grid origin (row 42, col 42), i.e. on Rua Doutor Beltrao's true midpoint. This overrides whatever street/block classification would otherwise apply there. The 3x3 size and centering are a PLACEHOLDER for the entrance-tower building footprint - level design/art should reposition or resize it (e.g. set back from the street centerline instead of straddling it) once the actual tower asset is authored.",
